    "updated_at": "2021-04-21T18:49:42Z",
    "body": "I can confirm that it is due to EOL before building, I cloned the repository and created a release build, and I did not have the issue (I didn't have to change line endings because I have git keep unix style line endings even on windows) but when I ran\r\n```sh\r\nfind . -type f -exec unix2dos {} \\;\r\n```\r\nin the repository, to simulate if git had actually converted to crlf on clone, the issue came up again.\r\n\r\nNow I don't know anything about CI, but it seems to me like the build machine could be configured to not convert the line endings, and that could fix the issue for zsh and bash on windows, based on the experience I've had here. BTW I did test this \"fixed\" build on powershell (not powershell core, I don't have the permissions to be able to install that) and it worked just fine there as well.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
